From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 16:34:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the timer and GIC
 maintenance interrupts

The dtsi lacks two private interrupts of the A733: the hypervisor virtual
timer, PPI 12, as the fifth arch timer interrupt, and the GIC maintenance
interrupt, PPI 9, which KVM's virtual GIC needs. Add both.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted at EL2 on two boards; arch_timer runs on
the EL2 virtual timer (INTID 28), its interrupt has fired on all eight
CPUs, and KVM initializes the vgic with its maintenance interrupt.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 31c6e7e023c2..4937ff109db2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -110,7 +110,8 @@ timer {
 		interrupts = <GIC_PPI 13 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
 			     <GIC_PPI 14 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
 			     <GIC_PPI 11 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
-			     <GIC_PPI 10 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			     <GIC_PPI 10 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+			     <GIC_PPI 12 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 	};
 
 	soc@0 {
@@ -175,6 +176,7 @@ gic: interrupt-controller@3400000 {
 			interrupt-controller;
 			reg = <0x03400000 0x10000>,
 			      <0x03460000 0x100000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_PPI 9 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 		};
 
 		mmc0: mmc@4020000 {
